---
import BoxScheleton from "../components/ui/BoxScheleton.astro";
---

{/* 2. The Problem Section */}
<section class="py-24 md:py-32">
  <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-4">
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-2 gap-16 items-center">
      <div class="order-2 lg:order-1">
        <div class="relative aspect-square max-w-md mx-auto">
          <div
            class="absolute z-10 -top-10 -right-8 bg-white border border-red-100 shadow-xl rounded-2xl p-4 hidden md:flex items-center gap-4 animate-bounce-slow"
          >
            <div
              class="w-10 h-10 rounded-xl bg-red-50 flex items-center justify-center"
            >

                    <span
                      class="material-icons-round text-red-500 animate-pulse"
                      >error</span
                    >
            </div><div>
              <div
                class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wide"
              >
                Accessibility Score
              </div><div class="text-xl font-bold text-red-500">
                34% <span class="text-xs font-medium text-red-300">Poor</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-blue-600/5 rounded-full blur-3xl">
          </div>
          <div
            class="relative glass p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-200 shadow-2xl"
          >
            <h4
              class="text-sm font-bold text-slate-500 uppercase tracking-widest mb-6"
            >
              Current Reality
            </h4>
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <BoxScheleton title="Bad alt text is worse than no alt text." type="seo" />
              <BoxScheleton title="Missing Alt Text" type="error" />
              <BoxScheleton title="The alternative text is uninformative" type="warning" />
              

              <p
                class="text font-serif text-slate-500 italic font-medium leading-relaxed"
              >
                "Most plugins deliver generic guesses that can be worse than
                having no alt text at all."
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="order-1 lg:order-2 space-y-8">
        <h2 class="text-5xl font-serif leading-[1.1]">
          Thousands of images.<br />
          <span class="italic text-slate-400">No time. Real legal risk.</span>
        </h2>
        <div
          class="space-y-6 text-slate-500 text-lg font-light leading-relaxed"
        >
          <p>
            If you run a modern WordPress site, you have hundreds or thousands
            of images. You know alt text is <span
              class="text-slate-900 font-bold">mandatory</span
            > (accessibility + SEO), but you keep postponing it because it’s repetitive
            and time-consuming.
          </p>
          <ul class="space-y-4">
            <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-red-500 mt-1">❌</span> Generic or incorrect descriptions
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-red-500 mt-1">❌</span> Confusing credit systems
            </li>
            <li class="flex gap-3 items-start">
              <span class="text-red-500 mt-1">❌</span> Results that damage screen-reader
              experiences
            </li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-neutral-900 font-semibold text-2xl pt-4">
            That’s not automation. That’s a lottery.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
